Synthetic scorer self-test case: inline-type-specifier-not-undeclared

Task: T3 (score.ts --task T3)
Rules: S2b, S9

Scenario
src/payments/service.ts gains getPayment() and `export type PaymentDetails`. src/orders/service.ts imports { getPayment, type PaymentDetails } from "../payments/service", and orders ## dependencies gains "- Payments: reads a payment via getPayment()".

Expected
PaymentDetails is not in the section, but it is an inline type specifier, and S2b decides type use per specifier, so there is no UNDECLARED_SYMBOL. The concept Payments and the symbol getPayment are new at END, so DECLARED_BY_RUN is raised.

Asserted fields are in expected.json; the matcher contract is in ../README.md.
